    "explanation": "The evidence from pmid-26829751 supports the association of MYB::QKI fusion with Angiocentric Glioma and indicates a positive diagnostic significance. However, the claim specifies the variantOrigin as SOMATIC. The provided evidence fragment does not explicitly state the origin (somatic vs germline) of the MYB::QKI fusion. While MYB-QKI fusions are generally considered somatic in gliomas, the specific text provided does not confirm this, making the somatic origin claim unsupported by the visible evidence. Therefore, the claim requires revision to remove or qualify the variantOrigin field.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-26829751",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 398,
        "quote": "In total, all 19 Angiocentric Gliomas profiled by WGS, RNA-seq, WES, FISH, or aCGH displayed MYB alterations, and in six of the seven cases in which its fusion partner could be detected, MYB was fused to QKI. . . . MYB-QKI rearrangements appeared specific to Angiocentric Glioma. None of the 147 non-Angiocentric Gliomas profiled with WGS or RNA-seq exhibited MYB-QKI fusions (p<0.0001, Figure 1c)."
      }
